# ==============================================================================
# Hardened Tor Configuration for AdGuard Home DNS Fortress & Proxy Gateway
# Default Location on Windows: %APPDATA%\tor\torrc or C:\AdGuardHome\tor\torrc
# ==============================================================================

# ─── Core Network & Ports ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SocksPort: SOCKS5 proxy on localhost with destination address/port isolation
# prevents stream correlation across different DNS resolvers and applications.
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050 IsolateDestAddr IsolateDestPort

# DNSPort: Local UDP DNS server provided by Tor for resolving .onion virtual IPs
# and serving as fallback Tor resolver on port 5350.
DNSPort 127.0.0.1:5350

# ControlPort: Loopback control interface for watchdog automated circuit rotation (SIGNAL NEWNYM).
# To enable authenticated rotation, generate a password hash by running:
#   tor.exe --hash-password "YourSecurePassword"
# and uncomment HashedControlPassword below:
ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
# HashedControlPassword 16:XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# Restrict SOCKS access strictly to local machine loopback interface.
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1
SocksPolicy reject *

# ─── Client Mode & Anti-Leak Hardening ──────────────────────────────────────
# ClientOnly: Do not act as a relay, bridge, or directory server under any condition.
ClientOnly 1

# SafeLogging: Scrubs all IP addresses and user data from Tor log output.
SafeLogging 1

# GeoIPExcludeUnknown: Avoid routing through relays whose country cannot be verified.
GeoIPExcludeUnknown 1

# StrictNodes: If 0, allows Tor to fallback if specific country constraints cannot be met.
StrictNodes 0

# ExcludeNodes: Optional. Uncomment to exclude relays located in jurisdictions known for mass interception:
# ExcludeNodes {cn},{ru},{ir},{by},{kp}

# ─── Onion Routing & Virtual IP Mapping ─────────────────────────────────────
# AutomapHostsOnResolve: Returns synthetic IPv4 addresses for .onion queries so
# standard DNS clients and AdGuard Home can route .onion requests without errors.
AutomapHostsOnResolve 1
AutomapHostsSuffixes .onion,.exit

# VirtualAddrNetworkIPv4: Subnet range used to map .onion synthetic addresses.
# Must be a private range that does not collide with local LAN.
VirtualAddrNetworkIPv4 10.192.0.0/10

# ─── Performance & Circuit Stability ────────────────────────────────────────
# NumEntryGuards: Maintain 3 stable entry guards to balance path diversity and guard pinning defense.
NumEntryGuards 3

# CircuitBuildTimeout: Timeout in seconds before abandoning an unresponsive circuit attempt.
CircuitBuildTimeout 10

# KeepalivePeriod: Send keepalive probes every 60s to prevent NAT state timeouts on firewalls.
KeepalivePeriod 60

# NewCircuitPeriod: Check every 30s whether a new circuit should be spawned.
NewCircuitPeriod 30

# MaxCircuitDirtiness: Re-use circuits for a maximum of 1800s (30 minutes).
# (Using lower values like 180s creates unnecessary relay churn and high DNS latency spikes).
MaxCircuitDirtiness 1800

# ─── Traffic Analysis Resistance ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ConnectionPadding: Defends against traffic analysis by adding packet padding between relays.
ConnectionPadding 1

# EnforceDistinctSubnets: Ensures no two relays in the same 16-bit subnet are used in one circuit.
EnforceDistinctSubnets 1

# ─── Forensic & Storage Resistance ──────────────────────────────────────────
# AvoidDiskWrites: Keeps state in RAM to protect SSD endurance and prevent forensic artifacts on disk.
AvoidDiskWrites 1

# ─── SOCKS Protocol Safety ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TestSocks: Keep at 0 to avoid unnecessary loopback port testing.
TestSocks 0

# WarnUnsafeSocks: Emit warnings if an application attempts unencrypted hostname resolution over SOCKS4.
WarnUnsafeSocks 1

# ─── Censorship Circumvention (Bridges / Pluggable Transports) ───────────────
# If Tor direct connection is blocked by your ISP, enable bridges below:
# UseBridges 1
# ClientTransportPlugin obfs4 exec C:\Program Files\Tor\PluggableTransports\obfs4proxy.exe
# Bridge obfs4 <IP>:<PORT> <FINGERPRINT> cert=<CERT> iat-mode=0
